class:: TemporalCentroid
summary:: Energy-weighted position within the recent envelope
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Amplitude

description::
The energy-weighted mean time of the rolling RMS envelope is sum(t[i] * e[i].squared) / sum(e[i].squared), where t is measured from the oldest frame boundary in seconds. An event moving toward the older edge lowers this value.

Frames contain nonoverlapping RMS measurements. Output stays zero until a complete observation window is available, then updates once per RMS frame. Silence returns zero. Runtime cost is linear in windowTime/frameTime per update; there is no callback allocation. These descriptors are rolling summaries and do not segment individual events. Formulas are independently implemented from standard weighted moments and linear regression.

The nearest vanilla building block is link::Classes/Amplitude::, which tracks instantaneous level; this UGen summarizes its recent distribution in time.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time observation duration, 2*frameTime through 10 seconds. Rounded up to whole RMS frames.

argument:: frameTime
Initialization-time RMS frame duration, 0.001 through 0.1 seconds.

argument:: floorDB
Silence floor in dBFS, clipped to -160..0. Used by dynamic complexity and dB regression; temporal moments use the original energy.

returns::
Seconds from the beginning of the observation window.

examples::
TemporalCentroid calculates the energy-weighted temporal center-of-mass within a rolling observation window (in seconds). Plucks with sharp attacks have an early temporal centroid (~0.05 s), while back-heavy swells produce late centroids. In this example, the temporal centroid controls a dynamic reverse swell envelope and filter sweep, accentuating front-heavy plucks vs. back-heavy sustaining notes. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: displays real-time temporal centroid in seconds.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("plucks.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic pluck fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(1.5);
            var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.4), trig);
            Pluck.ar(WhiteNoise.ar * env, trig, 0.2, 1/220, 2.0, 0.3)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var centroid = TemporalCentroid.kr(source, windowTime: 0.5, frameTime: 0.005);
        var centLag = centroid.lag(0.08);
        var swell = (centLag / 0.5).clip(0, 1);
        var filtered = RLPF.ar(source, swell.linexp(0, 1, 300, 3500), 0.3);
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + (filtered * 0.25);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, centLag.clip(0, 0.5)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Temporal Centroid", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 0.5, "s");
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

